WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.132
The request is about fifty
million dollars to refresh

2
00:00:03.132 --> 00:00:07.037
distribution point hardware across
about fifteen hundred offices.

3
00:00:07.037 --> 00:00:09.823
That's thirty-three thousand
dollars per office,

4
00:00:09.823 --> 00:00:14.349
nearly twice the cost of a fully loaded
server at the program's planning prices.

5
00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:17.754
Configuration Manager's own
limits say the estate needs

6
00:00:17.754 --> 00:00:21.375
about twenty-four distribution
points, not fifteen hundred.

7
00:00:21.375 --> 00:00:23.927
So the position is
simple: defer the refresh,

8
00:00:23.927 --> 00:00:28.109
pending a network modernization
assessment, because the same problem

9
00:00:28.109 --> 00:00:31.937
can be solved for about ten million
dollars in first-year capital.

10
00:00:31.937 --> 00:00:35.900
The next slide lists what has to be
answered before any money moves.
